<title>GERMANY: Philips to close German plant.</title>
<headline>Philips to close German plant.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German subsidiary of Philips NV, the Dutch electronics group, said on Tuesday it would close its radio manufacturing plant in Krefeld and will move production to Poland and Singapore.</p>
<p>The decision will put 240 of the plant's 350 employees out of work.</p>
<p>It does not affect production of components for television sets, video recorders and satellite-receiver systems at another plant in Krefeld where 360 people are employed, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
